      "problem": "Find the solution to $\\log\\left(x \\right) - \\log \\left( 2 \\right) = 1.$",
      "worked_solution": "The logarithms share the same base, so we can combine them using the quotient rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{log}⁡(x)-\\operatorname{log}⁡(2) & =1 \\\\ \\operatorname{log}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}) & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the equation for $x$ using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{10}^{\\operatorname{log}⁡(x/2)} & ={10}^{1} \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & =10 \\\\ x & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$",
